    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero">
      <div>
        <h1>Life doesn't always ask permission before it changes.</h1>
        <p class="sub">How to rebuild confidence, find direction, and move forward when life changes.</p>
        <p class="by">By Ashwik Bire</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href="https://amzn.in/d/0elSxaV1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get it on Amazon</a>
          <a class="btn alt" href="#frameworks">See the frameworks</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <figure class="cover" style="margin:0 auto">
        <img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Cover of The Quiet Strength by Ashwik Bire" width="640" height="1024">
      </figure>
    </section>
  </main>
</div>

<section class="moments" aria-labelledby="m-h">
  <div class="wrap grid">
    <h2 id="m-h">Written for the middle of it.</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A job ends.</li>
      <li>A relationship shifts.</li>
      <li>A plan fails.</li>
      <li>And you start to wonder if you're still capable of building the life you wanted.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="frameworks" id="frameworks">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Real frameworks, not empty motivation.</h2>
    <p class="intro">Four tools you can use on an ordinary, difficult day. Pick one to see how it works.</p>
    <div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Frameworks">
      <button role="tab" id="t0" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="p0">Circle of Control</button>
      <button role="tab" id="t1" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="p1" tabindex="-1">Action Ladder</button>
      <button role="tab" id="t2" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="p2" tabindex="-1">Mistake Recovery</button>
      <button role="tab" id="t3" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="p3" tabindex="-1">Life Audit</button>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="p0" aria-labelledby="t0">
      <h3>The Circle of Control</h3>
      <p>Change gets harder when you spend your energy on what you can't control. Sort it into three circles.</p>
      <ul class="steps">
        <li><b>What I control</b><span>My actions, effort, boundaries, habits, decisions and response.</span></li>
        <li><b>What I can influence</b><span>Relationships, opportunities, conversations, reputation and some outcomes.</span></li>
        <li><b>What I cannot control</b><span>Other people's decisions and everything that has already happened.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="p1" aria-labelledby="t1" hidden>
      <h3>The Action Ladder</h3>
      <p>When you're struggling to begin, climb one rung at a time.</p>
      <ul class="steps">
        <li><b>1. Think</b><span>Clarify what you actually want to do.</span></li>
        <li><b>2. Prepare</b><span>Identify what you need.</span></li>
        <li><b>3. Start</b><span>Take the smallest practical action.</span></li>
        <li><b>4. Repeat</b><span>Do another small action tomorrow.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="p2" aria-labelledby="t2" hidden>
      <h3>The Mistake Recovery Framework</h3>
      <p>When something goes wrong, four steps turn the mistake into information.</p>
      <ul class="steps">
        <li><b>1. Acknowledge</b><span>Name what happened accurately. Don't exaggerate it or minimize it.</span></li>
        <li><b>2. Understand</b><span>Ask why it happened: planning, information, emotion, communication or a missing skill.</span></li>
        <li><b>3. Repair</b><span>Fix what can be fixed and accept what can't be changed.</span></li>
        <li><b>4. Adjust</b><span>Decide what you'll do differently next time.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="p3" aria-labelledby="t3" hidden>
      <h3>The Life Audit</h3>
      <p>Before changing your life, understand your current one. Take a blank page and divide it into eight areas.</p>
      <ul class="audit">
        <li>Work</li><li>Health</li><li>Relationships</li><li>Money</li><li>Learning</li><li>Environment</li><li>Rest</li><li>Meaning</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="fine">For each area, ask what is working, what is not, what needs attention and what can wait. The goal is awareness, not perfection.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="inside" id="inside">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>A book you work through.</h2>
    <p class="lead">Seven chapters of honest, no-fluff writing. Chapters close with reflection exercises and a short takeaway, so each idea turns into something you do.</p>
    <ol class="chapters">
      <li><h3>When Life Changes Without Warning</h3><p>Start with reality, focus on what you can control and choose one useful step.</p></li>
      <li><h3>The Person You Become in Difficult Times</h3><p>A hard experience is not a permanent identity.</p></li>
      <li><h3>The Power of Small Steps</h3><p>When confidence is low, make the task smaller. Then begin.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Learning to Trust Yourself Again</h3><p>Self-trust is built quietly, one kept promise at a time.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Finding Direction When You Feel Lost</h3><p>Start with your values, explore before you commit and don't confuse urgency with clarity.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Building a Life That Feels Like Yours</h3><p>A meaningful life is built from ordinary choices.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Keep Going, But Do Not Forget to Live</h3><p>Bring it all together without losing the life you're building.</p></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="quote">
  <div class="wrap">
    <hr class="rule">
    <blockquote>You do not need to know exactly where the road ends. You only need enough clarity to take the next step.</blockquote>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Start where you are.</h2>
    <p>If you're rebuilding confidence, searching for direction, or just trying to take the next right step, this book meets you there.</p>
    <a class="btn" href="https://amzn.in/d/0elSxaV1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Get the ebook on Amazon</a>
  </div>
</section>

